WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:03.020
So today I want to talk to you about a molecule which,

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:07.180
when it was first isolated, was called "Very Fast Death Factor".

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:13.720
Now this molecule is a really potent toxin, and it's found in pond scum.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:20.140
The green, sort of gloopy algae stuff that you find sometimes on freshwater ponds.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.260
It's actually not algae that makes
this, it's called cyanobacteria.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.460
And that green, it turns out, is kind of
really important for this molecule.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:32.940
As it turns out, the molecule itself is unstable to light.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:38.960
So nature's clever, it didn't really - it wants a toxic molecule, for some reason, in that cyanobacteria,

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:42.380
in that algal bloom, but it
didn't want to spread too much.

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:47.280
So as soon as you take the molecule out of that, it becomes destroyed by light.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.480
But nonetheless, don't let this fool you. This is a very, very dangerous molecule.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:56.100
So I've got nearly 5 grams in this round bottom flask here.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.300
That would be enough to kill around 350 people.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:02.769
This is a seriously toxic molecule.

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:08.920
Now luckily, for everyone involved, this is actually in a protected form,

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:12.160
this molecule you see here in this flask, this compound.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.360
BRADY: What does that mean?

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:15.330
So, it's got a safety catch on it.

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:17.890
It's got something called a "protecting group".

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:25.720
And it completely kills the reactivity of one atom in this molecule, the nitrogen atom.

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:31.740
And that atom is a key to the biological response that it will provoke.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:35.280
So if we quickly put that one down...

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:44.260
Here is a molecular model of anatoxin-a, which is the "Very Fast Death Factor".

00:01:44.300 --> 00:01:47.820
It was renamed because that was thought not to be particularly scientific,

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:52.560
but I quite like "Very Fast Death Factor", it does what it says on the tin, essentially.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:55.240
So here is that key nitrogen.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:58.820
So it turns out it's the nitrogen and this oxygen over here,

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:02.300
and that distance, which is the key to its
biological activity.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:08.900
It fits a certain receptor that one of your natural neurotoxins triggers.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:13.600
So this molecule is a toxin,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:21.440
and what it does and why it's called "Very Fast Death Factor" is that it paralyzes somebody who ingests it,

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:28.080
be that an animal, a cow, a rabbit, bird, or whatever that's drinking from the pond,

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:31.640
or somebody who drinks or swims in the
pond.

00:02:31.640 --> 00:02:34.840
And it works really quickly, thus the
name, "Very Fast Death Factor".

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:41.360
Turns out that a lot of potent toxins
actually work very slowly. It's an agonizing death.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:47.180
This works very, very quickly, a matter of minutes rather than hours or days.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:52.080
What this does is it stops your brain communicating with your muscles.

00:02:52.090 --> 00:02:57.470
So nerves have two functions really. One, they tell muscles and your body to move -

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:03.440
be that breathe, which is part of - you know, you're on autopilot, you don't think about breathing,

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:08.820
but every few seconds, your brain's saying
"breathe in, breathe out, breathe in, breathe out."

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:11.890
It does it automatically - or move your
muscles.

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:16.080
So if you stop any of those signals, then obviously, your muscles stop.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:19.050
And if you stop breathing, you're gonna die pretty quick.

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:23.340
Obviously this compound is a very dangerous compound, so why on earth

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:27.650
would we be interested in making this and
analogues of this compound?

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:33.990
Well it turns out that it could be a good treatment for Alzheimer's disease.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.580
If you imagine a nervous system as a long piece of electrical wire,

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:40.860
and every now and again along that wire
you get, just like you do at home,

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:44.970
a plug and a socket where two bits of wire join.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:49.360
Now in electricity, the plug and the
socket are made of metal,

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:52.760
and the electrons can hop from one to the other, and there's no problem.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:57.400
In nervous transmission there is a little gap in-between the plug and the socket.

00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:03.660
And there's little molecules called "neurotransmitters" which come out of one end, they swim across the gap,

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:08.290
and they trigger the response in the other
end of the "synapse", as it's called.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:11.060
And then the electrical signal goes on again.

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:17.740
Now obviously you don't want those electrical signals to be on all the time. So the little molecule comes back out,

00:04:17.880 --> 00:04:20.960
and there's a Pacman-type molecule which comes and munches those up.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:28.240
To make sure that, you know, the response is gone, we now need to get rid of those and wait for the next signal.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:36.700
Now in certain conditions like Alzheimer's disease, your normal neurological condition degrades some more.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.820
They're called "neurodegenerative diseases".

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:43.980
The nerves in your brain don't work properly, and the problem is

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:49.580
that you get too many of these Pacman molecules taking up too many of those transmitters.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:54.200
And so your nervous system, your
brain isn't working properly.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:05:00.380
Now it could be that molecules like this,
which are able to disable these Pacman molecules,

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:06.920
could be very useful leads for treatment of Alzheimer's disease and other neurodegenerative diseases.

00:05:06.940 --> 00:05:11.480
So that's why, as chemists, we're interested in these things.

00:05:12.560 --> 00:05:16.260
We're not interested, obviously, in killing 350 people.

